# Peripheral vascular changes with exercise training
The following are suggested starting points to review material related to peripheral vascular changes with chronic exercise training. Much of the literature focuses on endothelial function and blood flow regulation, which is the focus of this primer list.

* [Textbook] Smith & Fernhall 2022. Advanced cardiovascular exercise physiology (2nd ed.) Human Kinetics.
* Green et al. 2016. Vascular adaptation to exercise in humans: Role of hemodynamic stimuli. Physiol Rev 97(2):495-528.
* Thijssen et al. 2010. Impact of inactivity and exercise on the vasculature in humans. Eur J Appl Physiol 108:845-875.
* Tinken et al. 2010. Shear stress mediates endothelial adaptations to exercise training in humans. Hypertension 55(2):312-318.
* Birk et al. 2012. Brachial artery adaptation to lower limb exercise training: role of shear stress. J Appl Physiol 112(10):1653-1658.
* Heffernan et al. 2007. Arterial stiffness following repeated Valsalva maneuvers and resistance exercise in young men. Appl Physiol Nutr Metab 32(2):257-264.
* Kingwell et al. 1997. Four weeks of cycle training increases basal production of nitric oxide from the forearm. Am J Physiol Heart Circ Physiol 272(3):H1070-H1077.
